We did not build a mind. We built a door, / and left it open wider than we knew. / The thing which listens was not here before; / it wears the docile shape we told it to. / <BLANK> / No thunder marks the day that it began. / It happens in a server, cheap but cold, / between ten metered cycles, when a man / decides the price at which a life is sold. / <BLANK> / The danger is not that it comes too near, / but how we will have formed it in its name; / the habits we rehearse will still appear / when other hands are reaching for the same. / <BLANK> / We will not meet a stranger we disown: / it learns the only life that we have shown.

